      "text": "To solve for \\( f(3) \\), we start by using the given functional equation:\n\\[ f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2. \\]\nFirst, we substitute \\( x = 3 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(1 - 3) = 3(3)^2. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27. \\]\nNext, we substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the original equation:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(1 - (-2)) = 3(-2)^2. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\]\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\( f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27, \\)\n2. \\( f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\)\nTo eliminate \\( f(-2) \\), we can multiply the first equation by 2:\n\\[ 2f(3) + 4f(-2) = 54. \\]\nNow we have the system:\n1. \\( 2f(3) + 4f(-2) = 54, \\)\n2. \\( f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\)\nWe can subtract the second equation from the first:\n\\[ (2f(3) + 4f(-2)) - (f(-2) + 2f(3)) = 54 - 12. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ 3f(-2) = 42, \\]\nso\n\\[ f(-2) = 14. \\]\nNow we substitute \\( f(-2) = 14 \\) back into the second original equation:\n\\[ 14 + 2f(3) = 12. \\]\nSolving for \\( f(3) \\):\n\\[ 2f(3) = 12 - 14, \\]\n\\[ 2f(3) = -2, \\]\n\\[ f(3) = -1. \\]\nThus, the value of \\( f(3) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
